{"name":"Highlighter Pink","hex":"#ea5a79","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"highlighter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A marker pen used to highlight text.","A cosmetic product that reflects light, used to emphasize the contours of the face etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highlighter"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Highlighter","blocks":[{"text":"A highlighter, also called a fluorescent pen, is a type of writing device used to bring attention to sections of text by marking them with a vivid, translucent colour.\nA typical highlighter is fluorescent yellow, with the colour coming from pyranine. Different compounds, such as rhodamines are used for other colours."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highlighter","wikidata":"Q559350"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Markeerstift-01_%28xndr%29.jpg/500px-Markeerstift-01_%28xndr%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Markeerstift-01_